        <h1 class="font-typewriter text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl mb-6">
          Matcha latte near Sant Feliu de Guíxols: what's there and what's worth the detour
        </h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-mono leading-relaxed">

<p class="mb-4">Sant Feliu de Guíxols has plenty of cafés. On the seafront, near the market, by the port. Most of them have a "matcha latte" on the menu — order one and they'll make it. What varies is what that matcha actually is.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Five minutes away by car, in S'Agaró, is Dirty Rabbit. We opened in November 2024 with a menu built from scratch around specific suppliers. The matcha wasn't a marketing decision.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What makes a good matcha latte</h3>
<ol class="list-decimal list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>The ingredient matters more than most people expect. Ceremonial matcha has a completely different flavour profile from food-grade — smoother, greener, without the bitterness that makes a lot of people think they don't like matcha. What they don't like is usually that version of it.</li>
  <li>Dose counts. We use 2g per cup, the standard measure to get recognisable flavour without going overboard. There's an extra strong option if you want more intensity, for a little extra.</li>
  <li>Preparation: the matcha is whisked with cold water first, then the milk goes in. Skip that step and the powder clumps at the bottom. It's a detail you can't see but you notice.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What matcha you can order</h3>
<ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>Classic matcha latte — hot or iced, with plant milk available</li>
  <li>Orange matcha — with orange juice instead of milk (dairy-free, more refreshing)</li>
  <li>Extra strong — higher dose, for a little more</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Where to find a good matcha latte near Sant Feliu de Guíxols</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Dirty Rabbit is at Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275, S'Agaró — five minutes from Sant Feliu along the GI-682.</p>
<p class="mb-4">The matcha we use is from REQ Matcha, a project founded by a Japanese man who lives in Japan and travels to the plantations to select the tea directly. It comes to Barcelona and from there to us. Short chain, traceable.</p>
<p class="mb-4">In central Sant Feliu you'll find spots with sea views. If the matcha itself is what you're after, the detour to S'Agaró makes sense.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Why matcha is everywhere but good matcha is rare</h3>
<p class="mb-4">There's a simple economic reason: Japanese ceremonial matcha costs significantly more than generic green powder. If a café sells a matcha latte at the same price as a regular coffee, it's worth asking where the saving comes from.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Specialty coffee arrived late to the Costa Brava compared to Barcelona or Girona city. Matcha followed the same pattern. The places that took coffee seriously also took alternatives seriously. Not many in the area, but they're here.</p>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
<h2 class="font-typewriter text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-8 mt-16">Frequently asked questions about matcha latte near Sant Feliu de Guíxols</h2>
<div class="space-y-6">
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Is there anywhere in Sant Feliu de Guíxols that serves quality matcha?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Options for ceremonial matcha in Sant Feliu are limited. The nearest place with Japanese-origin organic matcha is Dirty Rabbit in S'Agaró, five minutes by car.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">How far is Sant Feliu de Guíxols from Dirty Rabbit?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">About 4–5 kilometres along the GI-682 towards Platja d'Aro. We're at Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275, S'Agaró.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Can I order the matcha latte with plant milk?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes. We work with plant-based options alongside dairy. Ask at the counter for availability.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Are you open year-round or just in summer?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">We opened on 1 November 2024 and have stayed open. We're not a seasonal spot, though hours may vary between high and low season.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Do you have a terrace at Dirty Rabbit?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes, a large terrace when the weather allows. Good morning light and WiFi available.</p>
</div>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
</div>
<h2 class="font-typewriter text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6 mt-12">About Dirty Rabbit</h2>
<p class="mb-4">We opened on 1 November 2024 in S'Agaró. Specialty coffee, properly made alternative drinks, and a place to stay in if you want.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Iwonka runs day-to-day with a clear rule on suppliers: if she can't explain where an ingredient comes from, it doesn't go on the menu. Matcha from REQ Matcha. Coffee from La Cabra. Bread from Origo Bakery.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Natural light in the mornings, WiFi, large terrace when the weather holds. The kind of place where you can work through a morning without anyone minding.</p>

